    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter May 18th with a balanced lineup, led by the high-upside pairing of **Yordan Alvarez** (71.77) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (68.64). **Yordan Alvarez** is our primary engine today; while facing a lefty in Rojas, his elite 0.425 xwOBA overrides the platoon disadvantage, providing significant ceiling potential against a high-xERA opponent. Meanwhile, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** remains a high-priority start despite a suboptimal 8th-order slot. His elite speed profile is vital in our pursuit of stolen bases, and the matchup against Sproat offers a favorable platoon split that sustains his daily efficiency score well above the \"Strong\" threshold. Both **Colt Keith** (68.01) and **Trea Turner** (67.98) provide reliable top-of-the-order production, with **Colt Keith** benefiting from a slow delivery matchup against Cecconi that should create ample opportunities for him to swipe bags.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved balancing the depth of our middle infield against the static value of our outfielders. **Hyeseong Kim** (47.43) narrowly secures the UTIL spot, though his value is dragged down by a 9th-order assignment and a defensive matchup against King. We considered a swap to promote bench depth, but with **Kyle Schwarber**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Gary Sanchez** unavailable due to lineup status and **Zac Veen** still working through his stint in Albuquerque, we are locked into our current configuration. Risks remain, particularly with **Christian Yelich** (51.70), whose score was suppressed by a poor platoon dynamic against Imanaga. We will monitor the weather closely; should conditions worsen in the games featuring **Dillon Dingler** (48.56) or **Junior Caminero** (56.55), we must remain disciplined with our game cap management, as both sit near the lower bounds of our \"Strong\" start threshold.",
